{"id":"b2016a44e2de38ce","group":"92","path":"92/92-df-propositional-axiom.md","title":"Propositional Axiom","display":"df-propositional-axiom — Propositional Axiom","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems","book_abbrev":"92","label":"92-df-propositional-axiom","aliases":["92-df-propositional-axiom"],"display":"df-propositional-axiom — Propositional Axiom","depends_on":["[[92-df-formula]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"92"},{"key":"label","html":"92-df-propositional-axiom"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>92-df-propositional-axiom</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-propositional-axiom — Propositional Axiom"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5a1bd470754681a7\" href=\"?note=5a1bd470754681a7\" title=\"92-df-formula\">92-df-formula</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_G\">\\(\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_G\\)</span> (formulas, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5a1bd470754681a7\" href=\"?note=5a1bd470754681a7\" title=\"92-df-formula\">92-df-formula</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PropAx}_G\">\\(\\mathrm{PropAx}_G\\)</span> (definition-target axiom set)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}propositional\\text{-}axiom}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PropAx}_G\\coloneqq\\{\\;&amp;\n\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi),\\\\\n&amp; (\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\chi))\\to((\\varphi\\to\\psi)\\to(\\varphi\\to\\chi)),\\\\\n&amp; (\\neg\\varphi\\to\\neg\\psi)\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi),\\\\\n&amp; (\\varphi\\land\\psi)\\to\\varphi,\\quad(\\varphi\\land\\psi)\\to\\psi,\\quad\n\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to(\\varphi\\land\\psi)),\\\\\n&amp; \\varphi\\to(\\varphi\\lor\\psi),\\quad\\psi\\to(\\varphi\\lor\\psi),\\\\\n&amp; (\\varphi\\to\\chi)\\to((\\psi\\to\\chi)\\to((\\varphi\\lor\\psi)\\to\\chi))\n\\mid\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_G\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}propositional\\text{-}axiom}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PropAx}_G\\coloneqq\\{\\;&amp;\n\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi),\\\\\n&amp; (\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\chi))\\to((\\varphi\\to\\psi)\\to(\\varphi\\to\\chi)),\\\\\n&amp; (\\neg\\varphi\\to\\neg\\psi)\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi),\\\\\n&amp; (\\varphi\\land\\psi)\\to\\varphi,\\quad(\\varphi\\land\\psi)\\to\\psi,\\quad\n\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to(\\varphi\\land\\psi)),\\\\\n&amp; \\varphi\\to(\\varphi\\lor\\psi),\\quad\\psi\\to(\\varphi\\lor\\psi),\\\\\n&amp; (\\varphi\\to\\chi)\\to((\\psi\\to\\chi)\\to((\\varphi\\lor\\psi)\\to\\chi))\n\\mid\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_G\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>关键符号：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>命题公理：命题逻辑的公理</li>\n<li>前三组模式给出经典的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg,\\to\">\\(\\neg,\\to\\)</span> 核心</li>\n<li>后六组模式分别给出原始联结词 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\land,\\lor\">\\(\\land,\\lor\\)</span> 的引入与消去性质</li>\n<li>与 Modus Ponens 合用时，这是一套适用于本书原始联结词语言的经典 Hilbert 命题演算公理基</li>\n<li>也可选用其他等价的有限公理基，但不能在把 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\land,\\lor\">\\(\\land,\\lor\\)</span> 视为原始符号时只保留 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg,\\to\">\\(\\neg,\\to\\)</span> 的模式而不另给定义或公理</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"92-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"5a1bd470754681a7